{"id":"8feaeac2-e56c-44ba-a665-1cec244e8e34","type":"level","createdDate":"2026-09-09T23:11:29.507Z","createdBy":"bill.marsland@codeninjas.com","lastModifiedDate":"2026-09-09T23:11:29.507Z","lastModifiedBy":"bill.marsland@codeninjas.com","attributes":{"tags":["CREATE"],"title":"Level 3","sequence":3,"activity":{"id":"7c5e2f7b-5200-4d0d-be12-a8cee0ca56fb","type":"activity","sequence":1,"group":{"id":"80f2e681-8593-4903-81b7-95afb2ba023e","type":"solve","name":null,"sequence":4,"subgroups":[{"id":"bfc0712b-c340-47ec-9515-9342e3b40500","type":"subgroup","sequence":1,"name":"solve 1","steps":[{"id":"d7463947-b9a8-4490-8b1b-64ddd4647bc4","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ Did you use the documentation for help with setting the sprite’s velocity and animation?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Ask the ninja:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>❓ Did you set the Player sprite’s y-velocity in the A button pressed event?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Code should be added to set the Player sprite’s y-velocity (vy) to a negative value inside the A button pressed event under <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">// game events</strong>.</p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/o5v4yrgh.v02.png\"></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>❓What value might the Player sprite’s x-velocity be set to so that it is pushed to the right of the screen?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Code should be added to set the Player sprite’s x-velocity to a positive value inside the Player/Fan <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">onOverlap</strong> event under <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">// game events</strong>.</p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/ohvlsuyi.1ub.png\"></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>❓ What function and asset should be used to animate the Fan sprite?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>The <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">runImageAnimation</strong> function should be added under <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">// sprite animation</strong>, with the air sprite and the <strong>airAnim</strong> animation asset used as arguments.</p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/c2n3j5yg.znw.png\"></p>","instructions":"<p>Fix the bugs in the code to create a working platformer game!</p><p><br></p><p>The Player sprite should be able to jump onto a platform, and should be pushed to the right by the Fan sprite, after overlapping it.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>The Fan sprite should be animated so that air appears to be blowing.</p><p><br></p><p>Use the functions in the code menu and the code completion tool to create a working version of this 2D platformer project!</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null}],"title":"Debugging 2D Tilemap Movement","project":{"editor":{"filters":[],"searchBar":true},"source":{"text":{"main.ts":"namespace SpriteKind {\n    export let Fan = SpriteKind.create()\n}\n\n// project set up\ntiles.setCurrentTilemap(tilemap`level1`)\n\n// sprite set up\nlet dustMite = sprites.create(assets.image`dustMite`, SpriteKind.Player)\ntiles.placeOnTile(dustMite, tiles.getTileLocation(0, 0))\ndustMite.ay = 500\ncontroller.moveSprite(dustMite, 100, 0)\nscene.cameraFollowSprite(dustMite)\n\nlet fanBlades = sprites.create(assets.image`fanBlades`, SpriteKind.Fan)\nlet air = sprites.create(assets.image`airImage`, SpriteKind.Fan)\ntiles.placeOnTile(fanBlades, tiles.getTileLocation(39, 4))\ntiles.placeOnTile(air, tiles.getTileLocation(40, 4))\n\n// sprite animation\n\n// game events\ncontroller.A.onEvent(ControllerButtonEvent.Pressed, function () {\n\n})\n\nsprites.onOverlap(SpriteKind.Player, SpriteKind.Fan, function (sprite, otherSprite) {\n    controller.moveSprite(sprite, 0, 0)\n})\n","pxt.json":"{\n    \"name\": \"Untitled\",\n    \"description\": \"\",\n    \"depen